  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For an array AAA of size NNN, define f(A)f(A)f(A) as ∑i=1N−1(Ai⊕Ai+1)\\sum_{i = 1}^{N - 1} (A_i \\oplus A_{i + 1})∑i=1N−1​(Ai​⊕Ai+1​), i.e. (A1⊕A2+A2⊕A3+…+AN−1⊕AN)(A_1 \\oplus A_2 + A_2 \\oplus A_3 + \\ldots + A_{N - 1} \\oplus A_N)(A1​⊕A2​+A2​⊕A3​+…+AN−1​⊕AN​).\n\nHere ⊕\\oplus⊕ represents the Bitwise XOR operator. f(A)f(A)f(A) is defined as 000 when N=1N = 1N=1.\n\nGiven integers NNN and MMM, consider the arrays AAA satisfying ∣A∣=N|A| = N∣A∣=N and 0≤Ai≤M0 \\le A_i \\le M0≤Ai​≤M. Let SSS denote the maximum possible value of f(A)f(A)f(A).\n\nFind the number of arrays AAA satisfying the constraints, such that f(A)=Sf(A) = Sf(A)=S, modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains 222 integers NNN and MMM.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of arrays with f(A)=Sf(A) = Sf(A)=S modulo 998244353998244353998244353, where SSS denotes the maximum possible value of f(A)f(A)f(A).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N,M≤1081 \\le N, M \\le 10^81≤N,M≤108"
    ],
